  "reason": "The original assertion 'self attention --[computes]--> weight matrix' is rejected because it conflates the intermediate calculation of attention scores (weights) with the final output generation. Self-attention computes a set of attention scores which are then applied to value vectors to produce an output representation, rather than simply computing a static 'weight matrix' as its sole result. The term 'weight matrix' in this context refers to dynamic attention weights derived from Q-K similarity, distinct from static parameter matrices. To preserve causal strength and precision, the target concept should be refined to 'attention scores' or the relation must specify the computation of these scores before aggregation.",
